beyond necessity."  In other words, if two systems both work and one is
simpler, the simpler one is probably the one with better predictive power.
(Closer to true-to-fact.)  Somebody (Kuhn?) stated that as scientific
models get more and more complex they are leading up to a paradigm-shirt, a
scientific revolution, going back to simple models again.

